Subject: Re: detecting RApache
Message-ID: <ih1R4vrIg6Y.48QOZFoZTPAJ@rapache.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <ih1R4vrIg6Y.cHbbWNmC6WkJ@rapache.groups.google.com>
References: <ih1R4vrIg6Y.cHbbWNmC6WkJ@rapache.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rapache/c/ih1R4vrIg6Y/m/48QOZFoZTPAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Yes. Depending on how apache was packaged you can either call the
apache binary or apachectl shell script with the -M argument and grep
for R_module. For instance on Ubuntu (my machine):

$ apache2ctl -M 2>&1 | grep R_module
 R_module (shared)

reveals that indeed rApache is installed.

Jeff

